 "title": "GIS / Newton County, Indiana",
 "text": "GIS / Newton County, Indiana\nSkip over navigation\nNewton County\nThe Official Government Website for Newton County, Indiana\nDocuments | Site Tools\nSearch\nSearch Submit\nStart Content\nToggle Menu\nHome\nAbout Community Events\nCounty Demographics\nDocument Center\nEmployment Opportunities\nEvents Calendar\nResident Information\nCourthouse Assessor\nAuditor\nClerk\nCourts\nProbation\nProsecutor\nRecorder\nTreasurer\nCourthouse Directory\nGovernment Center Adult Education\nBuilding Department\nCoroner's Office\nCounty Commissioners Commissioners Meeting Schedule\nMeet Your Commissioners\nCounty Council Council Meeting Schedule\nMeet Your Council Members\nHealth Department\nPark Board\nPurdue Extension\nRecycling\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nVeteran's Service Officer\nWIC\nWorkOne\nCounty Facilities Ambulance Service\nAnimal Control\nCommunications Center\nDepartment Child Services\nDivision of Family Resources\nEmergency Management Agency\nHighway Department\nMaintenace Department\nMap of County Offices\nSearch Locations by Name\nSurveyor's Office\nSheriff Dept In Remembrance\nNewton County Jail\nContact Ask a Question\nBoards & Commissions Board of Zoning Appeals\nDrainage Board\nPlan Commission\nPlat Commission\nCounty Departments A-G Ambulance Services\nAnimal Control\nAssessor's Office\nAuditor's Office\nBuilding Department\nClerk of Courts\nCoroner's Office\nEconomic Development\nElections & Voting\nEmergency Management Agency\nEmergency Medical Services\nGIS Services\nCounty Departments H-Z Health Department\nHighway Department\nMaintenance Department\nNewton County Extension Office\nProbation Department\nProsecutor's Office\nRecorder's Office\nRecycling\nSheriff's Department\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nSurveyor's Office\nTreasurer's Office\nZoning\nVeteran's Service Officer\nSubmit an Online Form\nView the County Staff Directory\nEmployee Resources Doculivery\nEmployee Webmail\nEmployment Application\nYou are here: Home » Departments » GIS\nGIS\nWelcome to the Newton County GIS Home Page. The information you find here will enhance your map researching capabilities by integrating county offices and department's information under one system. By utilizing our GIS website, you have the capability of viewing and querying a wide variety of data layers. You also have the ability to print street maps of our County, Townships, and Towns.\nWhat is GIS? GIS is an abbreviation for geographic information system, a computer system to create, analyze, report, and map data geographically.\nResponsibilities: Newton County GIS has geospatial data available in shapefiles, geodatabase, PDF maps, web maps, and web applications. Part of the department’s responsibility includes maintaining digital maps and creating data layers for Newton County. Please do not hesitate to reach out with any data needs or questions!\nAvailable Data Layers include Townships, Sections, Parcels, Addresses, Lots, Subdivisions, Aerial Photography, Contours, Address Points, Street Centerlines, Rights of Way, Drains, Tiles, Precincts, Flood Zones, Soils, Zoning, and much more!\nClick he re to go to t he Newton County GIS Beacon website\nUseful Links\nServices\nUseful Links\nNewton County Street Map | Newton County Town Maps | Newton County Township Maps |\nServices\nGIS Services – Beacon | Search for My Tax Information | |\nContact Us\nGIS Department\n310 N 7th St\nKentland, IN 47951\nGet Directions\n|\nLocation/Facility Details\nPhone: (219) 474-6081\nStaff Directory\nOffice Hours:\nMonday-Friday 8:00 a.m.-4:00 p.m.\nTopics of Interest\nPrintable GIS Maps\nMore Information\nDocument Center Useful Links\nLocations\nServices Index\nSite Design and Content Copyright © 2026 Newton County, IN\nSite Design and Content Management by\nCORE Business Technologies\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility Statement\nTerms of Use",
